description:
AckOnErrorSender exposes rule_id and dtag as public mutable fields, allowing callers to corrupt sender state mid-transmission.

**Location:** /Volumes/Attic/Desktop/Projects/crates/schc/src/fragment/ack_on_error.rs:127-130

```rust
pub struct AckOnErrorSender<'a, const M: u8, const N: u8, const T: u8, const TILE: usize> {
    payload: &'a [u8],
    /// Rule ID for this fragmentation session.
    pub rule_id: u8,
    /// DTAG for correlating fragments (0 if T=0).
    pub dtag: u8,
```

**What goes wrong:**
```rust
let mut sender = AckOnErrorSender::new(&payload, 5, 0, 1000)?;
sender.start()?;
for frag in sender.iter() { send(frag); }

// Bug: caller accidentally overwrites rule_id
sender.rule_id = 99;  // compiles!

// ACKs for rule_id 5 will now be rejected - session wedged
```

The rule_id and dtag are set once at construction and must not change during a session. Making them pub allows accidental or malicious mutation.

**Fix:** Change to private fields with public getters:
```rust
rule_id: u8,  // private
dtag: u8,     // private

pub fn rule_id(&self) -> u8 { self.rule_id }
pub fn dtag(&self) -> u8 { self.dtag }
```
